{"shortDescription":"Central European currencies extended losses on Tuesday, with Hungary's forint easing the most, reeling from a firmer U.S. dollar ahead of a Federal Reserve interest-rate decision, rising oil prices and U.S. Treasury yields.","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Central European currencies extended losses on Tuesday, with Hungary's forint easing the most, reeling from a firmer U.S. dollar ahead of a Federal Reserve interest-rate decision, rising oil prices and U.S. Treasury yields."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"Monday's shock – a post-weekend surge in energy prices, a rise in the 10-year U.S. Treasury yield to 5%, and a stronger U.S. dollar – hit CEE markets hard, weakening currencies and sharply repricing rates higher across the curve,\" ING said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"Although risk-off sentiment is likely to persist today, higher front-end rates should help cushion currencies against further losses and create scope for stabilisation.\""]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The forint ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX:EURHUF","text":"FX:EURHUF"}}," weakened 0.4% to 367.00, while the Polish zloty (EURPLN) was 0.2% weaker at 4.3455 per euro at 0730 GMT."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"CEEMEA currencies also weakened as higher energy prices and developed-market rate expectations supported the dollar. The moves were consistent with broader pressure on emerging-market carry as investors moved toward USD liquidity ahead of major central-bank meetings,\" Morgan Stanley said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The main event of the week in the region will be Thursday's Czech National Bank interest-rate decision where the bank is expected to keep its benchmark rate at 3.75%."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The crown ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol